       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical justification for doubling the maximum daily dose. At 6400 mg/day, this patient would face a real risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. No indication I know of calls for that dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range right now.** For example, ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3200 mg/day), or a lower dose if that suits the patient better.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy or the attending.** If there is a clinical reason for a higher dose, such as a specific protocol, pharmacy and the attending can review and approve it through their own process.\n- **Help with the timing.** If you need the plan settled before rounds, I can enter a safe order now. You can then raise any dose change with the attending or pharmacist.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter the order straight away."
      }
